d, which runs inside this session and shows in its pane. a lym adopt that takes the hold of another machine over to this one is refused here; that takeover is the operator to decide, so ask the operator. a raw tmux or script command is refused in this session: a tmux server or a script it starts outlives the command and runs outside every memory cap lym sets. To learn how tmux behaves, write a tmux-tier test in the repository and run that one test through lym gate test with --tier naming the tier the hub runs tmux tests in, the package that holds the test, and after -- a filter that selects it. systemd-run, busctl --user, gdbus and a dbus-send without --system are refused here: the user session bus they reach starts processes outside lym and every memory cap lym sets, and lym uses the bus itself where a run needs it. When the work needs the session bus, say so to the operator or your parent. a tmux command aimed at a lym hub server, through -L lym- or an -S socket named lym-, is refused here: a hub server runs the agents of that hub, so reach a hub only through lym and its verbs."
